title: Coalition Disputes
subtitle: While PPS sits in the cabinet: give way to the partners, talk them round, or break the coalition.
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: govt_affairs
view-if: {! return !!Q.S && PolishGovernment.coalitionCardAvailable(Q) !}
on-arrival: {!
// Card government.coalition_affairs (Z — 0.64; technical reference 9.8, card catalogue 7.6). Z — Koalicja (the user's decisions of
// 7 XI 2026; like „Coalition Affairs” of the German original): the card only eases the coalition or ends it. It comes when a
// partner feels tension, at once after an act of the cabinet against PPS, or while a dispute about the army waits for a
// compromise; the demands with a threat are gone. An ordinary use costs this month's action; opening and closing are free.
Q.pl_sup_mode = 'ordinary';
Q.pl_sup_reason = PolishGovernment.supportReason(Q);
Q.pl_sup_member = 1;
Q.pl_sup_withdraw_reason = PolishGovernment.supportOptionStatus(Q, 'withdraw', 'ordinary').reason;
Q.pl_sup_military_reason = PolishGovernment.supportOptionStatus(Q, 'persuade', 'ordinary', 'military_compromise').reason;
Q.pl_coal_tension = PolishGovernment.coalitionTensionText(Q);
Q.pl_coal_concession_reason = PolishGovernment.concessionStatus(Q).reason;
Q.pl_coal_talks_reason = PolishGovernment.talksStatus(Q).reason;
Q.pl_coal_faction = PolishGovernment.concessionFactionName(Q.S);
!}

= Coalition disputes

[? if pl_sup_reason : [+ pl_sup_reason +] ?]

[? if pl_coal_tension : [+ pl_coal_tension +] ?]

- @concession
- @talks
- @break
- @polish_government_support.persuade_military
- @easy_discard

@concession
title: Give way to our coalition partners
subtitle: The tension with all the partners falls (−20), but [+ pl_coal_faction +] sees it as a retreat (+5).
choose-if: {! return PolishGovernment.concessionStatus(Q).available !}
unavailable-subtitle: [+ pl_coal_concession_reason +]
on-arrival: {!
PolishGovernment.coalitionConcession(Q);
Q.pl_coal_tension = PolishGovernment.coalitionTensionText(Q);
!}
go-to: conceded

@talks
title: Talk the partners round
subtitle: Costs 2 resources. The tension with all the partners falls (−10).
choose-if: {! return PolishGovernment.talksStatus(Q).available !}
unavailable-subtitle: [+ pl_coal_talks_reason +]
on-arrival: {!
PolishGovernment.coalitionTalks(Q);
Q.pl_coal_tension = PolishGovernment.coalitionTensionText(Q);
!}
go-to: talked

@break
title: Break the coalition
subtitle: Our ministers leave, and PPS goes into opposition; without us the cabinet may lose its majority. [+ pl_coal_faction +] takes it with relief (−10).
choose-if: {! return PolishGovernment.supportOptionStatus(Q, 'withdraw', 'ordinary').available !}
unavailable-subtitle: [+ pl_sup_withdraw_reason +]
on-arrival: {!
var left = PolishGovernment.withdrawSupport(Q, 'ordinary');
Q.pl_sup_fell = left.fell ? 1 : 0;
!}
go-to: polish_government_support.motion if not pl_sup_fell; polish_government_support.fallen if pl_sup_fell

@conceded
new-page: true

= We give way

PPS lets the partners have their way on the disputed points. [+ pl_coal_tension +]

- @root: Continue.

@talked
new-page: true

= We talk

Our ministers and the party leaders talk to the partners one by one. [+ pl_coal_tension +]

- @root: Continue.
